> Checking the search geometry

>> Diagonal versus rotated quadratics

Use eigenvalues (2,200), centre zero and start (3,-4), once aligned with axes and
once rotated by pi/4. Both minima are zero; only the orientation changes.
Nelder–Mead keeps its default .05 simplex displacement and 2000-iteration budget;
CMA-ES keeps its seed-42 six-offspring default and 500-generation budget.
Plot the running best evaluated trial versus objective-call index. These are not
accepted-mean trajectories, and different evaluation counts are not elapsed-time
measurements. Covariance adaptation's mechanism is assessed on declared inputs,
not treated as an unconditional rotation-invariant global convergence claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_derivative_rotation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o = dm::optim;
  o::QuadraticObjective aligned({2, 200}, {0, 0}),
      rotated({2, 200}, {0, 0}, 0, std::numbers::pi / 4);
  std::vector<dm::graphics::RPlot> plots;
  for (auto* f : {&aligned, &rotated}) {
    const auto a = o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(*f, o::NelderMead(), {3, -4}),
               b = o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(*f, o::CMAES(), {3, -4});
    plots.push_back(
        o::optimization_comparison(*f, {a, b}, {"simplex", "CMA-ES"}, "value", 0, true)
            .title(f == &aligned ? "Axis-aligned stiff bowl" : "Same eigenvalues, rotated bowl"));
    std::print(
        "{}\n\nNelder-Mead\n\n{}\n\nCMA-ES\n\n{}\n\n",
        f == &aligned ? "aligned" : "rotated",
        a.summary().to_md(7),
        b.summary().to_md(7));
  }
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(plots[0])
      .add(plots[1])
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/opt_derivative_rotation.svg");
}
```
