>> Multimodal surfaces and local basins

The bumpy surface is (x0-three)^2+(x1+one)^2+five*sin(x0)*cos(x1). It is bounded
below by minus five, but the best value found by a finite search is not proved to
be its global minimum. The figure uses this *lower bound* as its declared reference.
Rastrigin is sum_j(x_j squared+ten*(one-cos(two*pi*x_j))); every term is nonnegative,
so its global minimum zero at the origin is exact.

Compare default simplex and seed-42 CMA-ES with seed-42 PSO on these two surfaces.
The first start is (0,0), the second (3,-4). PSO spreads its 40 initial particles
through a box, [-8,8] for bumpy and [-5.12,5.12] for Rastrigin; CMA starts with SD .5
around its mean, while the simplex is initially local. The domains, initial
coverage, populations and budgets differ, so this illustrates search behaviour
rather than a controlled universal ranking. Small best values and different basin
endpoints are retained in the tables.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_derivative_basins.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o = dm::optim;
  std::vector<dm::graphics::RPlot> plots;
  for (const std::string family : {"bumpy", "rastrigin"}) {
    o::SmoothBenchmark        f(family);
    const std::vector<double> start =
        family == "bumpy" ? std::vector<double>{0, 0} : std::vector<double>{3, -4};
    const double bound = family == "bumpy" ? 8 : 5.12;
    const auto   a     = o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(f, o::NelderMead(), start),
               b       = o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(f, o::CMAES(), start),
               c       = o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(
                   f,
                   o::PSO(),
                   start,
                   std::vector<double>(2, -bound),
                   std::vector<double>(2, bound));
    plots.push_back(
        o::optimization_comparison(
            f, {a, b, c}, {"simplex", "CMA-ES", "PSO"}, "value", family == "bumpy" ? -5 : 0, true)
            .title(
                family == "bumpy" ? "Bumpy: reference is lower bound -5"
                                  : "Rastrigin: known minimum zero"));
    for (const auto* run : {&a, &b, &c}) {
      auto g = f.gradient(run->coordinates);
      std::print(
          "{}\n\n{}\n\nSeparate analytic gradient norm: {:.6g}.\n\n",
          family,
          run->summary().to_md(7),
          std::hypot(g[0], g[1]));
    }
  }
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(plots[0])
      .add(plots[1])
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/opt_derivative_basins.svg");
}
```
