>> Keep the complete seed and population scan

Fix seeds {one,two,seven,42,123} before inspection and compare CMA-ES's default six
offspring with 40 offspring, both capped at 500 generations. Every row is retained,
including a local-basin result. A larger population spends more evaluations per
generation and changes the adaptation constants. Five outcomes cannot establish
reliability across arbitrary seeds or objectives; hitting a known zero within a
numerical tolerance is a finite observed success, not a proof about the algorithm.
The plot floors only its displayed loss at 1e-14.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_derivative_seeds.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o = dm::optim;
  o::SmoothBenchmark               f("rastrigin");
  const std::vector<std::uint64_t> seeds{1, 2, 7, 42, 123};
  std::vector<double>              index, small, large;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < seeds.size(); ++i) {
    index.push_back(i);
    for (std::size_t population : {0, 40}) {
      o::CMAESOptions opt;
      opt.seed            = seeds[i];
      opt.population_size = population;
      const auto run      = o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(f, o::CMAES(opt), {3, -4});
      (population ? large : small).push_back(std::log10(std::max(1e-14, run.checked_value)));
      std::print(
          "seed={}, offspring={}\n\n{}\n\n",
          seeds[i],
          population ? population : 6,
          run.summary().to_md(7));
    }
  }
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                  .line(index, small, "six offspring", {40, 100, 190})
                  .points(index, small, "six", {40, 100, 190}, 4)
                  .line(index, large, "forty offspring", {190, 100, 35})
                  .points(index, large, "forty", {190, 100, 35}, 4)
                  .title("CMA-ES: declared seed and population scan")
                  .x_label("seed")
                  .x_ticks(index, {"1", "2", "7", "42", "123"})
                  .y_label("log10 final loss, floor 1e-14")
                  .y_limits(-15, 6)
                  .legend({"six offspring", "forty offspring"}, {{40, 100, 190}, {190, 100, 35}});
  plot.size(850, 490).save_svg("build/opt_derivative_seeds.svg");
}
```
